description:
Builds a gridded population-exposure dataset: loads a climate dataset and a population dataset, multiplies the climate variable by the population surface per pixel and time step (population aligned to the climate grid by nearest-neighbour interpolation), and publishes the result as a new GeoZarr dataset. For example PM2.5 x WorldPop gives population-weighted PM2.5 exposure (units person*ug/m3).

The output_dataset_id must have a registered dataset template on the instance (sync: {kind: static} with a display block). Run as a batch job (Zarr output is batch-only):

{
  "x": {
    "process_id": "population_exposure",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "cicero_pm25_daily",
      "population_dataset_id": "worldpop_population_1km_yearly",
      "output_dataset_id": "cicero_pm25_pop_exposure",
      "variable": "pm25_pop_exposure",
      "temporal_extent": ["2023-01-01", "2023-01-31"]
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
